<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Winhold hikes half year EPS, no div.</title>
<headline>Winhold hikes half year EPS, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  5.8	   vs 4.1</p>
<p>    After tax		 3.82	  vs 2.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.42	  vs 4.69</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.54	  vs 0.84</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.25	  vs 0.98</p>
<p>    Turnover		  157.87	vs 130.87</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.02	  vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Winbel Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said no interim dividend had been declared. Shareholders were directed to a cautionary dated June 13 concerning talks between a unit of subsidiary Inmins Ltd and outside shareholders. Directors said that if talks were successful they would have a material stabilising effect on Inmins. The effect on the earnings per share of Imnins, Winhold and Winbel Ltd was not ascertainable until negotiations were finalised.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
